;; Card 9ce04add: jobs.lib.targets ranks candidates with go-to's own prices (damage weight, health scale): fell-tree with two trees picks the one
;; whose walk is not past a hostile. Tree A is nearer (9.5 east) with a zombie (NoAI, helmeted) at its foot; tree B is farther (10.5 west), clear. The body stands 9 off the zombie, outside the hostile-near radius, else fell-tree waits.
;; The body must have seen the zombie before the job starts, else it ranks the trees without it and walks to tree A.
;; Should-succeed: tree B is felled first (its base log gone), tree A stands. The live risk is the margin between the prices.
{:defaults
 {:tags [:forestry :fell-tree :planner]
  :time :any
  :mobs :keep
  :plot {:height 10}
  :blocks [[:fill [22 0 16] [22 4 16] "oak_log"] [:fill [20 4 14] [24 6 18] "oak_leaves[persistent=true]"] [:fill [22 4 16] [22 5 16] "oak_log"]
           [:fill [2 0 16] [2 4 16] "oak_log"] [:fill [0 4 14] [4 6 18] "oak_leaves[persistent=true]"] [:fill [2 4 16] [2 5 16] "oak_log"]]
  :body {:at [12.5 0 16.5] :settle-s 2 :inventory [["iron_axe" 1]] :effects [["resistance" 600 4]]}
  :limit-s 120}
 :cases
 [{:name "tree-past-a-zombie-is-felled-after-the-clear-one"
   :body {:yaw 270}
   :act [[:summon "zombie" [21.5 0 16.5] "{NoAI:1b,equipment:{head:{id:\"minecraft:iron_helmet\",count:1}}}"]
         [:until-seen {:entity "zombie"} 10]
         [:job (jobs.forestry.fell-tree {:radius 20})]]
   :expect [{:event {:source :job :kind :completed} :within-s 100 :of-job true}]
   :after [[:not-block [2 0 16] "oak_log"] [:block [22 0 16] "oak_log"]]}]}
